--Description: Fix PostgreSQL-specific parts in all remaining queries so they work in SQLite.
--             (1) Query flights involving Abakan — unchanged (plain SQL).
--             (2) Pull coordinates of every airport in those flights; wrap the UNION and put
--                 LIMIT after the whole UNION so SQLite applies it to the combined set.
--             (3) Compute great-circle (Haversine) distances; SQLite lacks point-array syntax,
--                 so longitude/latitude are parsed from the “(lon,lat)” text using SUBSTR/INSTR,
--                 and radians are obtained via *π/180.  Uses a CTE for clarity.
--             (4) Find the maximum of those distances with the same parsing logic.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2) All flights where Abakan (airport_code = 'ABA') is the point of departure or arrival
SELECT DISTINCT
       flight_id,
       flight_no,
       departure_airport,
       arrival_airport,
       scheduled_departure,
       scheduled_arrival
FROM   flights
WHERE  departure_airport = 'ABA'
   OR  arrival_airport   = 'ABA'
LIMIT 20
